The benchmark build uses the reviewed scalar CPU path under GCC 11.4:

* remove the unused C++23 <stdfloat> dependency;
* replace std::to_underlying with an explicit size_t conversion;
* use the existing scalar residual writer instead of the forced native-SIMD writer;
* replace diagnostic-only std::float64_t casts with double.

This patch does not alter partition selection, model evaluation, residual coding,
serialization, scalar decompression, or random-access semantics. The AVX2/AVX-512
paths remain outside this AlgorithmID and require separate admission.
